  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "British bakery executive Ross Warburton has argued that keeping profits in the business allows a family company to invest patiently. He welcomed experienced outside managers and independent directors, describing their scrutiny as a useful challenge to family decisions. The family name on the product, he believed, also imposed a personal responsibility for quality.\n\nHis work with young people included a long presidency of Bolton Lads and Girls Club. He later chaired the OnSide Foundation, which funds youth facilities. His own charitable trust supported that organisation and pledged funding to Oriel College, with the college pledge scheduled to be paid over four years.",
